# CTFX git flow

When updating a working branch `A` from `master`/`develop`:

1. Stay on branch `A`.
2. `git fetch` all remotes.
3. Branch `master`/`develop` into a temp branch `B`.
4. Merge `A` into `B`.
5. Reset `A` to `B`.
6. Delete `B`.
7. Continue on `A`.

Do not force-push unless the user explicitly asks.

# Merge request body

```markdown
## [Task Id](task-link) Task Title
### Summary of Changes
- details-commit-changes
### Checklist
#### Code is up to date
- [ ] Code is checked by checkstyle
- [ ] Latest code pulled from working branch (base-branch)
- [ ] All merge conflicts are resolved
- [ ] Source code is build/executed successful
- [ ] Source code is tested on local machine
- [ ] Source code is passed UT
#### Database changes
- [ ] No changes
#### Configuration change
- [ ] No changes
#### Library changed
- [ ] N/A
#### Task in Openproject/Jira/...
- [ ] Status updated
- [ ] Time logged
#### Acceptance criteria
- Refer [task-Id-of-QC](task-link)
```
